{"title":"Brinewater Ports","sub":"Predictive maintenance: a $3.5M promise","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Ports and shipping","geo":"Singapore","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"AI business case · bottleneck value · peak vs off-peak","prompt":"Brinewater runs a container terminal with 12 ship-to-shore cranes. A vendor offers AI that predicts crane breakdowns from sensor data, claiming it would cut unplanned downtime from 8% to 5% and add about $3.5M a year of container moves. It costs $1.2M to install and $0.4M a year to run. The terminal director asks for your view.","clarify":[{"q":"Crane operation?","a":"Each crane is available about 8,000 hours a year and moves about 30 containers an hour; each move earns about $40 of margin."},{"q":"Is the terminal full?","a":"For about four months a year (the peak season) ships queue and every crane hour is used. The rest of the year, cranes are often idle."},{"q":"Maintenance savings?","a":"Fewer emergency repairs and overtime would save about $0.6M a year."},{"q":"Other bottlenecks?","a":"None during peak; berths and yard have spare capacity."}],"structure":{"root":"Is predictive maintenance worth it for Brinewater?","branches":[{"head":"Extra crane hours","items":["Downtime reduction × hours"]},{"head":"Are those hours valuable?","items":["Only when cranes are the bottleneck"]},{"head":"Other savings","items":["Repairs, overtime, safety"]},{"head":"Costs","items":["Install","Running"]}]},"hypothesis":"Extra crane hours are only valuable when ships are waiting. Most of the year cranes are idle, so the vendor is probably overstating the value.","questions":[{"q":"Recreate the vendor's claim.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Hours saved: 12 cranes × 8,000 × (8% − 5%) = 2,880. Containers: × 30 = 86,400; × $40 = <b>$3.46M</b> a year.</p>"},{"q":"Which of those hours actually add moves?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.46pt\" height=\"171.36pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.46 171.36\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 171.36 L 388.46 171.36 L 388.46 -0 L 0 -0 L 0 171.36 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 35.3 133.76 L 381.26 133.76 L 381.26 11.792 L 35.3 11.792 L 35.3 133.76 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"120.916364\" y=\"133.76\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(91.561598 149.985) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-33\" d=\"M 2266 0 L 1613 0 L 128 4467 L 704 4467 L 1440 2214 L 1933 538 L 1965 538 L 2470 2214 L 3213 4467 L 3770 4467 L 2266 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" d=\"M 1786 -77 Q 1338 -77 1005 137 Q 672 352 486 739 Q 301 1126 301 1651 Q 301 2176 486 2563 Q 672 2950 1005 3164 Q 1338 3379 1786 3379 Q 2227 3379 2547 3171 Q 2867 2963 3040 2598 Q 3213 2234 3213 1766 L 3213 1523 L 838 1523 L 838 1370 Q 838 941 1097 656 Q 1357 371 1818 371 Q 2131 371 2364 518 Q 2598 666 2726 941 L 3091 678 Q 2931 346 2592 134 Q 2253 -77 1786 -77 z\nM 1786 2950 Q 1510 2950 1296 2822 Q 1082 2694 960 2467 Q 838 2240 838 1952 L 838 1907 L 2662 1907 L 2662 1978 Q 2662 2272 2553 2489 Q 2445 2707 2246 2828 Q 2048 2950 1786 2950 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" d=\"M 1056 0 L 544 0 L 544 3302 L 1056 3302 L 1056 2765 L 1082 2765 Q 1203 3046 1424 3212 Q 1645 3379 2016 3379 Q 2528 3379 2825 3049 Q 3123 2720 3123 2118 L 3123 0 L 2611 0 L 2611 2029 Q 2611 2470 2422 2694 Q 2234 2918 1862 2918 Q 1658 2918 1472 2851 Q 1286 