ink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p084e170f0e\"><rect x=\"35.3\" y=\"11.792\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Net yearly benefit, including maintenance savings and running costs ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Only during peak season, when ships are queuing: one-third of the year. Off-peak, a crane that would have broken down is simply replaced by an idle one.</p> <p>Valuable hours: 2,880 × 1/3 = 960; × 30 × $40 = <b>$1.15M</b>. Plus maintenance savings $0.6M, less $0.4M running: <b>$1.35M a year</b>.</p> <p>Payback on $1.2M: <b>0.9 years</b>. Still a good investment, but the extra moves are worth only a third of what the vendor claims ($1.15M vs $3.46M). On the same net basis as ours (adding maintenance savings, less running costs), the vendor's case would be $3.7M.</p>"},{"q":"How could Brinewater get more value from it?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Plan maintenance for the quiet months</b>, using the predictions to do repairs off-peak so cranes are fully available in peak season</li> <li>Negotiate the vendor's fee as a share of peak-season availability gains</li><li>Extend later to yard equipment if that becomes a bottleneck</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Invest, but expect about $1.4M of net yearly benefit, not the $3.7M the vendor's figures imply. Extra crane hours only add moves in the four-month peak, when ships queue; for the rest of the year cranes have spare time. Including $0.6M of maintenance savings, the system pays back in about 0.9 years. Use the predictions to shift maintenance into quiet months, and tie part of the vendor's fee to peak-season availability. Risk: sensor data quality on older cranes. Next step: pilot on the four busiest cranes.","great":["Rebuilds the vendor's figure","Values capacity only where it is the bottleneck","Includes maintenance savings and running costs","Finds a way to raise the value (shift maintenance off-peak)"],"id":78,"slug":"brinewater-ports"}